//// Decision 663 — A decorator is always a function, and `Annotation` goes: no type or enum is an annotation by implementing a behavior; `#[name(…)]` names a function whose first parameter is `syntax decl`, and the data an annotation carries is a record the decorator records with `compiler.setMeta`. There is no `Decorator` type (666): a decorator's name at build is a declaration handle.

import {compiler, io.terminal} from "std";
import {comptime.marks.mark, comptime.marks.audited, comptime.marks.Mark, comptime.marks.Audit};

#[mark(label: "x")]
#[audited]
type Widget(size: i32)

#[audited]
type Plain(size: i32)

pub fn main() -> void {
    terminal.print(comptime compiler.typeInfo(Widget).meta(Mark)?.label ?? "-");
    terminal.print(comptime compiler.typeInfo(Widget).meta(Audit)!.marked);
    terminal.print(comptime compiler.typeInfo(Plain).meta(Mark)?.label ?? "-");
    terminal.print(comptime compiler.typeInfo(Plain).meta(Audit)!.marked);
}
